.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt G0WM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm g0wm
.Nd a Wayland compositor with a built-in desktop
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Nm
.Fl c
.Nm
.Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Wayland compositor built on wlroots.
It has a bar, a runner, notifications and a system tray built in,
along with tiling, floating and tabbed layouts.
It started as a fork of dwl.
.Pp
Start it from a TTY or select it in your display manager.
The status text comes from standard input, so you can pipe a status script
into it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
your-status-script | g0wm
.Ed
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Turn on debug logging, including wlroots messages.
Logs go to standard error.
.It Fl c
Create a config file with the defaults if there isn't one yet.
An existing file is kept and read instead.
Print the resulting settings to standard output and report problems on
standard error, without starting a graphical session.
.Pp
Problems are reported with line numbers.
Read the messages even if the command exits successfully.
.It Fl v
Print the name and version to standard error and exit with a nonzero status.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Settings live in
.Pa ~/.config/g0wm/config ,
or
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/g0wm/config
when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set to a nonempty value.
Run
.Nm Fl c
to create the file.
.Pp
The format is scfg: each line has a setting and its value, braces group
settings into blocks, and a hash starts a comment.
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
windows {
    borderpx 2
    gappx 6
}

key logo+q spawn foot
button client logo+left moveresize move
.Ed
.Pp
Settings you leave out keep their defaults.
Bindings, rules and monitors keep theirs if you don't write any entries of
that kind.
Super+Shift+R reloads the file; some input changes need a restart.
.Pp
The default terminal is
.Xr foot 1 .
The default quit binding is Super+Shift+Escape.
.Sh STATUS TEXT
Each line read from standard input replaces the text in the bar.
There is no status script included.
.Pp
.Em ^c#RRGGBB^
sets the foreground colour and
.Em ^b#RRGGBB^
sets the background colour for the text that follows.
.Em ^d^
restores the default colours and
.Em ^^
draws a caret.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Directory containing the
.Pa g0wm/config
file.
If unset or empty,
.Nm
uses
.Pa $HOME/.config .
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The login session's runtime directory, used for the Wayland socket.
Must be set when starting the compositor.
.It Ev HOME
Used to find the config when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or empty.
.It Ev WLR_*
Backend, renderer and other wlroots options.
.It Ev XKB_* , XLOCALEDIR , XCOMPOSEFILE
Keyboard layout and compose settings used by libxkbcommon.
.It Ev XCURSOR_PATH
Directories to search for cursor themes.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
sets
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
for programs it starts.
When built with X11 support, it also sets
.Ev DISPLAY
for Xwayland clients.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.config/g0wm/config
.It Pa ~/.config/g0wm/config
User settings, read at startup and on reload.
A normal user install also creates this file if it is missing;
root and staged installs do not.
.It Pa /usr/share/wayland-sessions/g0wm.desktop
Display manager session entry for the system packages.
A default source install puts it in
.Pa ~/.local/share/wayland-sessions/ ,
which most display managers don't read.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr foot 1 ,
.Xr xkeyboard-config 7
.Pp
The source tree has the full settings reference in
.Pa docs/settings.md ,
build instructions in
.Pa docs/building.md
and help with common problems in
.Pa docs/troubleshooting.md .
.Sh BUGS
Report bugs at
.Lk https://github.com/frapank/G0wm/issues .
Include the version, distro, GPU, wlroots version, how to repeat it and
a debug log.
